-## iOS tab and navigation chrome
+*Board Editor:* `/editor` remains reachable via Explore on web for board route creation and hold-matrix editing. iOS does not provide hold-matrix authoring.
+
+*Explicit Non-Goals:* Boarded V1 explicitly **bans** chat, events, meetups UI, training plans, gym administration, marketplaces, and coaching analytics.
+
+## Destination definitions
+
+### 1. Feed (iOS Tab 1, Web `/app`)
+- The community publication feed of **completed climbing sessions**.
+- Default feed filter is **Following-only** (`following_only=true`).
+- Feed items represent full completed sessions, never detached single sends.
+- Geometry matches the approved Paper specification (`10 - Feed / Populated / iPhone`):
+  - 62 pt status + safe area.
+  - 56 pt header (Boarded wordmark in Cormorant Garamond, 44 pt notification bell with unread blue indicator).
+  - 673 pt scroll feed (58 pt author row + 479 pt media with Obsidian fade + 40 pt caption + 52 pt actions row + 44 pt next session preview hint).
+  - 49 pt tab bar + 34 pt bottom safe area.
+
+### 2. Explore (iOS Tab 2, Web `/explore`)
+- Discovery engine for climbing routes, crags, gyms, public boards, and fellow climbers.
+- Search with instant filtering by venue, discipline (sport, boulder, trad, board), and grade system.
+- Route cards show grade in Cormorant Garamond, route name, venue, rock type, height, terrain, and save status.
+- Saved routes filter (`saved_only=true`) allows climbers to review bookmarked routes.
+- Climber search finds public profiles with follower/following counts.
+
+### 3. Log (iOS Tab 3, Web `/log`)
+- Start, record, and close active climbing sessions.
+- Prominent central placement in navigation.
+- Real-time attempt recorder: Sent, Fell, Stopped.
+- Private session context: **Conditions (1..500 chars)** and **Notes (1..1000 chars)**.
+  - *Privacy guarantee:* Session conditions and notes are strictly private to the user. They are never implicitly leaked or published to the public Feed. The public share caption is a separate deliberate field.
+- Works offline; attempts queue locally and sync automatically when connectivity resumes.
+
+### 4. Activity (iOS Tab 4, Web `/activity`)
+- Community notifications and activity inbox.
+- Events: Likes, Comments, Follows, and Crew Sends.
+- Unread status indicated by a clear badge/dot; one-tap mark-as-read.
+- Tapping an activity opens the actor's public profile or navigates directly to the referenced post.
+- Not a duplicate of private attempt history.
+
+### 5. Profile (iOS Tab 5, Web `/profile`)
+- Climber identity: Avatar, username, full name, home area, and bio.
+- **Public profile vs. private logbook privacy separation:**
+  - **Public profile view (community):** Displays identity, follow counts, and public aggregates derived **solely from explicitly published session posts** (published session count, published sends). It strictly excludes unpublished session totals, private vertical volume, and private session notes.
+  - **Owner logbook view (authenticated climber):** Displays full lifetime private logbook statistics (lifetime private and published session totals, total vertical gain across all sessions, complete attempt send rate, and personal records) and historical logbook timeline.
+- Follower and following relationships and counts.
+- **Saved bookmarks tab (`route_bookmarks`):** Strictly owner-only; bookmarked routes are never publicly visible or disclosed on the climber's public profile.
+- Standard grouped settings list (account, privacy, units, grade system preferences).
+
